# `this.total += i` in a loop of a method, the instance out of sight. The read finds the slot filled and the walk's state holds what lay there; nothing runs between it and the store. The look at the
# slot that the store goes to takes that answer: in the typed copy of the loop (the second head) the slot is not asked again whether it is filled, nor read again.
